course: dictionary
lesson: 7839
title: Racism: unfair treatment because of race
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Racism is treating people badly because of their race or where their family comes from.» Read the clues around the word: treating people badly and because of their race. So racism means unfair, hurtful treatment of people for who they are, not for what they do.
explain: Racism can also be bigger than one person's actions. It can be unfair rules or systems in a society that disadvantage some groups because of race. Check the meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «Telling someone to go back where they supposedly came from is racist bullying.» The clue is bullying, so racist bullying means bullying that is unfair because of race.
explain: Racism is a word you cannot count, like kindness, so you say racism, not racisms. The adjective is racist, as in «racist bullying». When you meet a word like this, the clues in the sentence are your best guide, and a dictionary can confirm them.
fact: Racism means treating people unfairly, or thinking they are worse, because of their race, skin colour, nationality or ethnic group.
fact: Racism can also be unfair rules or systems in a society that disadvantage some groups because of race.
fact: «Racism» is uncountable: you say racism, not racisms.
fact: In many countries, racist acts are against the law.
fact: Common phrases: stand up to racism, fight racism, tackle racism.
exercise: «Never mock the shape of someone's eyes: that is racism, not a joke.» What does racism mean? | Playing a fast game | Being very tall | Telling a funny joke | *Treating people unfairly because of their race
exercise: «A real friend stands with him and tells a teacher.» What should a friend do when racism happens? | Copy the teasing | *Stand with the person and tell a teacher | Walk away and say nothing ever | Laugh along quietly
exercise: Which sentence uses racism correctly? | Racisms all went home early | *Many people stand up to racism | Racism is a good way to make friends | The racism sang a song
test: «Telling someone to go back where they supposedly came from is racist bullying.» What does racist bullying mean? | *Bullying someone unfairly because of where their family comes from | Playing a game of tag | Helping someone move house | Bullying a dog
test: What is the best thing to do when you see racism? | Join in to fit in | Share a post that makes fun of it | *Report it to a teacher and stand up for others | Say nothing and ignore it
exam: Which statement about racism is true? | Racism is a type of weather | Racism is a sport played in schools | Racism is a kind joke | *Racism is hurtful and treats people unfairly because of race
